FX  - The material described in the present study was collected during the KANADEEP 1 (30 Aug. -27 Sep. 2017) cruise, co-organised by the Museum national d'Histoire naturelle (MNHN) and Institut de Recherche pour le Developpement (IRD), as part of the "Tropical Deep Sea Benthos" (TDSB) and "Our Planet Reviewed" programmes. The authors are deeply thankful to Dr. Sarah Samadi (MNHN), one of the chief scientists of the KANADEEP 1 cruise, for processing the trawled/dredged material during the cruise and taking colour photographs included in Figs. 4 and 5, and to Dr Laure Corbari (MNHN) for providing an opportunity for HA and ZD, and multiple opportunities for AA, to visit and work on the precious decapod collection of the MNHN. Dr. Tomoyuki Komai (Natural History Museum and Institute, Chiba, Japan) kindly provided tentative identification (based on photographs) of hermit crabs. The study was financially supported by the Student Grant Project SGS04/PrF/20 of University of Ostrava (HA).
