FX  - The Comprehensive Marine Biodiversity Survey (CMBS) was jointly led by the National Parks Board and National University of Singapore, with generous contributions from Asia Pacific Breweries Singapore, Care-for-Nature Trust Fund, Keppel Care Foundation, Shell Companies in Singapore and The Air Liquide Group. We are greatly appreciative of the tremendous efforts made towards the collecting, sorting and preliminary identification of specimens by the CMBS team, visiting scientists, NParks staff and Blue Water volunteers. We are especially grateful to Charles Messing, Toshihiko Fujita, Shane Ahyong, Arthur Anker, Jim Lowry and Lee Yen-ling for identifying the commensals. Charles Messing also kindly verified the identification of crinoid specimens. Comments from an anonymous reviewer greatly improved the quality of this paper. A portion of this paper was presented at the 15th International Echinoderm Conference held in May 2015.
