TY  - JOUR
AU  - SHEPPARD, CRC
TI  - CORAL FAUNA OF DIEGO-GARCIA LAGOON, FOLLOWING HARBOR CONSTRUCTION
T2  - MARINE POLLUTION BULLETIN
LA  - English
AB  - Early descriptions of Diego Garcia atoll report a fairly poor coral cover on lagoon knolls. Following dredging and blasting for military construction in this very enclosed lagoon, a brief survey was made of the coral fauna on 6 knolls near the new anchorage. All showed a high diversity of species that compared well with nearby, unaffected atoll lagoons but had a very variable and low coral cover. The process of construction appears to have had no major or lasting effect on the coral diversity, and cover may not have changed as a result of the works. Oil or other toxic spillages remain a threat, and this survey forms a baseline in such events.
