TY  - JOUR
AU  - BAK, RPM
TI  - LETHAL AND SUBLETHAL EFFECTS OF DREDGING ON REEF CORALS
T2  - MARINE POLLUTION BULLETIN
LA  - English
AB  - Effects of dredging on a coral reef are described. Underwater light values at a depth of 12-13 m were reduced from about 30% to less than 1% surface illumination. Colonies of coral species which are inefficient sediment rejectors (Porites astreoides) lost their zooxanthellae and died. Calcification rates in Madracis mirabilis and Agaricia agaricites decreased by 33%. The period of suppressed calcification exceeds that of environmental disturbance.
